---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const repositoryPolicy =
  "https://github.com/the-pavels/verba/blob/main/PRIVACY.md";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | Verba"
  description="How Verba handles selected text, translation, proofreading, permissions, storage, and updates."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="shell nav-shell">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Verba home">
        <img src="/images/verba-icon.png" alt="" width="36" height="36" />
        <span>Verba</span>
      </a>
      <a class="button button-small button-dark" href="/">
        Back to Verba
        <span aria-hidden="true">↖</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="shell legal-shell">
      <header class="legal-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy and data handling</p>
        <h1>Your words stay yours.</h1>
        <p>
          Verba has no accounts, analytics, advertising, telemetry, or
          Verba-operated cloud synchronization.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="legal-summary-grid">
        <article>
          <span>Translation</span>
          <h2>On your Mac</h2>
          <p>
            Selected text is processed through Apple’s Translation framework.
            For short single words, a bounded nearby excerpt may be read and
            used only for on-device language detection. Verba does not send
            translations to a Verba-operated server.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Proofreading</span>
          <h2>Only when requested</h2>
          <p>
            Selected text is sent to OpenAI with your own API key only after an
            explicit proofreading command.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Storage</span>
          <h2>No text history</h2>
          <p>
            Verba does not keep selected text or results. Your API key is stored
            as a password item in macOS Keychain.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <article class="legal-copy">
        <section>
          <p class="legal-kicker">Selection capture</p>
          <h2>Accessibility, with a narrow purpose.</h2>
          <p>
            Verba uses macOS Accessibility permission to copy the text currently
            selected in the frontmost app. It snapshots your pasteboard,
            performs a short copy transaction, and restores the previous
            contents when it is safe to do so. Secure text fields and unsupported
            content are rejected.
          </p>
          <p>
            When translating a short single word, Verba may use a read-only text
            range query to inspect a small amount of nearby text. This does not
            alter the selection. The excerpt is used locally to identify the
            language, is never sent to Apple Translation or OpenAI, and is
            discarded when the action finishes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="legal-kicker">Proofreading and OpenAI</p>
          <h2>Your account. Your request. Your review.</h2>
          <p>
            Proofreading uses the OpenAI Responses API with the API key you
            configure. Requests set storage off, have strict size and timeout
            limits, and are not logged by Verba. Corrections are displayed for
            review; Verba never automatically replaces your writing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="legal-kicker">What stays on your Mac</p>
          <h2>Preferences, not prose.</h2>
          <p>
            Verba stores settings such as your target language, shortcuts, and
            optional update preference. It does not store your selections,
            translations, or proofreading results.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <p class="legal-kicker">Full technical policy</p>
          <h2>Transparency down to the details.</h2>
          <p>
            The full policy documents clipboard behavior, provider data
            handling, networking limits, update checks, local storage,
            uninstall steps, and current limitations.
          </p>
          <a class="button button-dark" href={repositoryPolicy}>
            Read the complete policy on GitHub
            <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="shell footer-grid">
      <a class="brand brand-footer" href="/">
        <img src="/images/verba-icon.png" alt="" width="32" height="32" />
        <span>Verba</span>
      </a>
      <p>Translate. Proofread. Carry on.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Footer navigation">
        <a href="https://github.com/the-pavels/verba">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/the-pavels/verba/releases/latest">Releases</a>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
